*** ABORTED DELIBERATELY -- NOT A FAILURE, AND NOT AUTHORITATIVE ***
This regression run was stopped by hand about 15 minutes in, with 1 of 2718 tests complete and no
count produced. The reason is recorded because stopping an authoritative run needs one:

  While it was running, a review of the frozen gate against the tests found THREE criteria that
  named quantities nothing asserted --
     C1 and C2 name "rho, rhoU, rhoE, p, T"; the tests asserted only the three conserved ones
     Group G names sum_P rhoU V; the closed-box test computed the momentum and only printf'd it
  A regression is authoritative only if the binaries were built from the exact source being
  reported (CLAUDE.md section 8). Letting this run finish and THEN fixing the tests would have
  produced a result describing source that no longer existed, and would have required running the
  whole thing again anyway. Stopping early cost ~15 minutes; finishing first would have cost the
  full run twice.

  Its declared prediction (35 tests / 2731 / 2669) is superseded: a 36th test was added afterwards.
  The authoritative run is 50_p17_8_regress.log, which declares 36 / 2732 / 2670.

No test failed in this run. Nothing was hidden by stopping it.

